ematological neoplasm", "Stress-Induced Leukocytosis from recent cold/illness: Constitutional symptoms (weight loss, fatigue) suggest a more persistent process than transient viral illness", "Metastatic Visceral Mass Syndrome: No localized findings or imaging evidence to support this mechanism at this stage"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional symptoms (fatigue, weight loss)", "Markedly elevated leukocyte count", "Elevated leukocyte alkaline phosphatase"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.17833764129900861, "posterior": 0.07385155400812424, "danger": 0.6, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Elevated LALP is more common in reactive leukocytosis, providing weak support for this diagnosis."], "evidence_against": ["The combined evidence from the analysis of elevated leukocyte alkaline phosphatase (LALP) and normal differential suggests reactive leukocytosis is less likely…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.4, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.5649736476352596, "posterior": 0.40943301542104094, "danger": 0.3, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Absence of splenomegaly/lymphadenopathy slightly disfavors chronic myeloproliferative neoplasm, as these are expected in some subtypes."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2", "B2.3", "B2.4"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.2, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["chronic myeloid leukemia", "polycythemia vera", "essential thrombocythemia", "primary myelofibrosis"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.18832454921175312, "posterior": 0.09139129808505377, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Normal differential with elevated LALP is less common in myeloid neoplasms with increased blasts, mildly reducing their likelihood."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B3.1", "B3.2", "B3.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.9, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute myeloid leukemia", "myelodysplastic syndrome with excess blasts", "chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis"]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.011, "danger": 0.8, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Normal differential and lack of lymphoid features are not typical of lymphoid neoplasms, moderately disfavoring this diagnosis."]}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Plasma Cell Disorder", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.025, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Normal calcium and creatinine are less supportive of plasma cell disorder, but insufficient to exclude it outright."]}, "kb_myeloid_neoplasm_with_in": {"id": "kb_myeloid_neoplasm_with_in", "label": "myeloid neoplasm with increased blasts / blast crisis (AML, MDS-EB, CML-BC)", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.0, "danger": 0.0, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B2.1": {"id": "B2.1", "label": "Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML)", "parent": "B2", "level": 2, "status": "